/* ============================================================
   AUDIO-DATA.JS — the three recordings, embedded
   ------------------------------------------------------------
   audio/voice.MP3, audio/potion.MP3 and audio/punch.MP3 as base64, so they
   are part of the script rather than three things to go and fetch.

   WHY EMBEDDED RATHER THAN FETCHED. Fetching worked over http and produced
   silence everywhere else, which is the worst way for audio to fail: nothing
   throws, nothing logs, the sound simply never arrives. A page opened from
   disk cannot fetch its own neighbours at all, and between a service worker,
   a case-sensitive host and an offline load there are several more ways for
   the request to come back empty. None of them can happen to a string.

   The cost is about 56KB of script for 42KB of audio. That is a fair price
   for three sounds that then work identically from disk, from localhost, from
   GitHub Pages and offline.

   TO REGENERATE after replacing a file in audio/: re-run the base64 step in
   the commit that introduced this file. The audio/ folder stays the source of
   truth; this is a build product kept in the repo because there is no build.
   ============================================================ */

